<%- include('partials/header') %>
    <div class="spread">
        <section class="sheet sheet--grid chapter-copy" id="about">
            <h1>About me</h1>
            <p>I like the moment when something that used to feel like a black box starts to make sense. In computer science, that usually means going a layer deeper and asking what the operating system or hardware is doing underneath.</p>
            <p>I’m pursuing my M.S. in Computer Science at Georgia Tech, where I finished my B.S. in May 2026. As the head TA for Operating Systems, I get to work through xv6 with students. Teaching makes me notice the steps I’ve started to take for granted, especially when someone asks a question I haven’t thought to ask in a while.</p>
            <p>At IBM, I worked on tools that make build failures easier to investigate. With Enoki, I’m working on making it easier for industry teams to find researchers. Both have made me think about how much time we spend figuring out where to look before we can get to the problem itself.</p>
            <a class="ink-link" href="/resume">Read my résumé <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
        </section>

        <section class="sheet chapter-copy about-side">
            <h2>Outside the classroom</h2>
            <p>I grew up in Medford, Massachusetts, where I spent time on my high school’s robotics team and co-captained its science team. A lot of what I enjoy now still comes down to trying something with other people and seeing what we learn along the way.</p>
            <p>Away from my computer, I like cooking and baking, playing piano, and learning K-pop choreography with friends. I enjoy the small progress you can feel in those things, like getting through a passage a little more smoothly or knowing by touch when a dough is ready.</p>
